  "question": {
    "text": "The mass of a spaceship is $1000 \\mathrm{~kg}$. It is to be launched from the earth's surface out into free space. The value of ' $\\mathrm{g}$ ' and ' $R$ ' (radius of earth) are $10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$ and $6400 \\mathrm{~km}$ respectively. The required energy for this work will be ;",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Kr7Bl",
      "text": "\n$6.4 \\times 10^{11}$ Joules\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "xg9hI",
      "text": "\n$6.4 \\times 10^8$ Joules\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jCI0h",
      "text": "\n$6.4 \\times 10^9$ Joules\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vsKw5",
      "text": "\n$6.4 \\times 10^{10}$ Joules",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "To launch the spaceship out into free space, from energy conservation,\n$\\frac{-\\mathrm{GMm}}{\\mathrm{R}}+\\mathrm{E}=0$\n$\\mathrm{E}=\\frac{\\mathrm{GMm}}{\\mathrm{R}}=\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{GM}}{\\mathrm{R}^2}\\right) \\mathrm{mR}=\\mathrm{mgR}$\n$=6.4 \\times 10^{10} \\mathrm{~J}$",
    "image": null
  },
